Lab: User ID controlled by request parameter with data leakage in redirect 

Goal:-  This lab contains an access control vulnerability where sensitive information is leaked in the body of a redirect response. To solve the lab, obtain the API key for the user carlos and submit it as the solution.
You can log in to your own account using the following credentials: wiener:peter 

Observation:- data is leaked when redirecting to login page
Steps to solve :- 
        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Login using given credentials
        Step3:- Go to my account
        step4:- in URL observe "web-security-academy.net/my-account?id=weinier"
        Step5:- change id from weinier to carlos
        Step6:- it will redirect you to login page 
        Step7:- while redirecting , interupt the request in burpsuit repeater. You will get the api for carlos
        Step8:- Submit the api to the server

Result:- Sensitive information (API key) of another user was disclosed in the response body during a redirect, allowing unauthorized access to protected data.

Root Cause:- The application fails to enforce authorization prior to generating the response, resulting in sensitive data leakage within a redirect response. This, combined with user controlled identifiers, leads to an IDOR vulnerability.

Fix:- Validate user authorization before retrieving or rendering sensitive data, and ensure redirect responses contain no confidential information. Implement proper object-level access control for all user specific endpoints.









